I wish to thank the hon. member for Calgary South for having given me notice of this question. The answer to the first part of the question is yes. In so far as the second part of the question is concerned, I must say that a technical group under the chairmanship of Dr. John Convey, director of the mines branch, will include: Dr. George Laurence of Atomic Energy of Canada Ltd.; a representative of the federal Department of National Health and Welfare;
66968-9-1134
Inquiries of the Ministry two representatives from the Alberta government; one representative of Richfield Oil Corporation, and one representative, as an adviser, from the United States atomic energy commission.

Mr. Chairman, I doubt if it would because section 2 (h) of the act defines a fishing vessel as follows:
-"fishing vessel" means any ship or boat or any other description of a vessel for use In a primary fishing enterprise, that has an engine for its propulsion, and includes the equipment affixed thereto 66968-9-115
Fisheries Improvement Loans Act for use in the operation thereof but does not include prescribed electronic equipment;
